{"type":"standard","title":"Ben Cline","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Ben Cline</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q4885439","titles":{"canonical":"Ben_Cline","normalized":"Ben Cline","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Ben Cline</span></span>"},"pageid":20182915,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Rep_Ben_Cline_Official_Photo_119th_Congress.jpg/330px-Rep_Ben_Cline_Official_Photo_119th_Congress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":413},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e3/Rep_Ben_Cline_Official_Photo_119th_Congress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":3360,"height":4200},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1372674076","tid":"6f3f61c5-a638-11f1-a0bd-9cc892e86a85","timestamp":"2026-09-01T19:07:54Z","description":"American politician (born 1972)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ben_Cline","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ben_Cline?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ben_Cline?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Ben_Cline"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ben_Cline","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Ben_Cline","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ben_Cline?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Ben_Cline"}},"extract":"Benjamin Lee Cline is an American politician and lawyer serving as the U.S. representative for Virginia's 6th congressional district since 2019. A member of the Republican Party, he represented the 24th district in the Virginia House of Delegates from 2002 to 2018.","extract_html":"<p><b>Benjamin Lee Cline</b> is an American politician and lawyer serving as the U.S. representative for Virginia's 6th congressional district since 2019. A member of the Republican Party, he represented the 24th district in the Virginia House of Delegates from 2002 to 2018.</p>"}